toDividedPowers -- Translates to divided power monomial basis from ordinary monomial basis
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        f1 = toDividedPowers f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * f, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * Outputs:
      * f1, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * f1, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

If f is a polynomial, or a matrix of polynomials, then f1 is the corresponding
object written in the divided power monomial basis, where for example $x^2$
denotes $x^{(2)}$

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[x,y]               |
|                                   |
|o1 = S                             |
|                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : 2*x^2 == toDividedPowers (x^2)|
|                                   |
|o2 = true                          |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note fromDividedPowers: fromDividedPowers, -- Translates from divided
    power monomial basis to ordinary monomial basis

Ways to use toDividedPowers:
============================

  * "toDividedPowers(Matrix)"
  * "toDividedPowers(RingElement)"

